    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`: `private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");`\n- After a successful `saveOwner(...)` (so the owner id is assigned), emit one audit line carrying the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n      owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n  ```\n\nThe line is logged only on the success path (after all validation/quota checks pass and the entity is persisted), matching the spec's \"on successful create.\" The `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` test \u2014 which captures the `AUDIT` logger and asserts a line contains the id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 passes, and the full suite is **BUILD SUCCESS** (1/1, 0 failures).",
